  "Question": "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of length \\(2\\) and an acute angle of \\(30°\\). What is the length of the side opposite this angle?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The opposite side equals the hypotenuse multiplied by the sine of the angle: \\(2\\times 1/2=1\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Thirty-degree right-triangle property\n\nIn a right triangle, the side opposite a \\(30^\\circ\\) angle is half the hypotenuse. The requested length is therefore \\(\\frac{2}{2}=1\\).",
